# This repository lives in HOME and deliberately tracks only configuration.
#
# HOME holds highly sensitive data — ~/.ssh private keys, ~/.claude credentials,
# service secrets, and (on Trillian) the Companion-derived index. None of that may
# ever enter git.
#
# The `*` default is therefore a safety measure: everything is ignored unless it
# is explicitly un-ignored below, so sensitive files cannot be staged by accident
# (not even by `git add -A`). Add new exceptions only with great care.

*
!.gitignore
!CLAUDE.md

# --- ~/.claude config --------------------------------------------------------
# Only hand-authored configuration. Everything else under .claude/ stays ignored
# by the `*` above: session transcripts, the memory store (personal notes),
# .credentials.json, history.jsonl, error-context/, shell-snapshots/,
# file-history/, backups/, uploads/, paste-cache/.
#
# settings.json is tracked and MUST stay secret-free. Machine-local secrets belong
# in .claude/settings.local.json, which is deliberately NOT un-ignored below.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/mcp.json
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**

# --- host configuration capture ----------------------------------------------
# Written by host-config/capture-host-config.sh (plan §4b, checklist A8). This
# is the only tree in HOME that is un-ignored wholesale, so the script carries
# the burden the `*` default normally carries: it records secret-bearing files
# as names and locations only, and runs a scanner over its staged output before
# anything reaches the index. See the DESIGN RULES header in that script.
!host-config/
!host-config/**

# --- systemd user units (added 2026-09-14) ----------------------------------
# Hand-authored unit files. These define how services start and were previously
# edited with no diff or revert path. Drop-ins under *.service.d/ are included;
# any secret a unit needs goes in a mode-600 EnvironmentFile that stays ignored.
!.config/
.config/*
!.config/systemd/
.config/systemd/*
!.config/systemd/user/
!.config/systemd/user/**
# Never track the runtime symlink farms systemd manages itself.
.config/systemd/user/*.wants/
.config/systemd/user/*.requires/
# Secrets referenced by units, never their values.
.config/art-studio/
*.env
!*.env.example

# --- crontab snapshot (added 2026-09-14) ------------------------------------
# cron has no file to track, so the crontab is exported here. It is a SNAPSHOT,
# not the live source: after `crontab -e`, re-run `crontab -l > .config/cron/crontab.txt`.
!.config/cron/
!.config/cron/**

# --- ~/bin (added 2026-09-14) -----------------------------------------------
# Hand-authored helper scripts. Symlinks into ~/work are tracked as symlinks;
# they resolve because every machine now uses the same ~/work root.
!bin/
!bin/**

# --- host-config -------------------------------------------------------------
# Already tracked since it was created; listed here only so the un-ignore is
# explicit alongside bin/ and .config/systemd/. Captured host configuration:
# unit copies, script copies, ollama overrides, secrets INVENTORY (locations
# only, never values).
!host-config/
!host-config/**
